Thalos, a 9th level priest is in Kittamagh's second hand bookstore; not
a bad little place to browse.  Looks like he can pick up a few 
useful items here.  But wait! A pesky jackal, easily disposed of.  Well,
Thalos was feeling a bit peckish, so he ate the corpse.

"The corpse will cost you 22906480 zorkmids!", Kittamagh said blandly.

"What?!", the priest cried, outraged.  "I refuse to pay!"

But Kittamagh was adamant.  "Either pay, or I'll call the Kops," he said.

"Not a chance, you thief!", exclaimed Thalos as he read a stolen scroll
of teleportation and vanished.  Alarm bells went off, but to no avail
as the wily priest escaped down the back stairs.






